// Hello-world simulation driver for a real minion module: the VPU tensor-A
// register file (clocked; wraps a preview/commit RF). This is the asserted
// sim smoke of the minion side of the suite; the whole-subsystem driver
// (vpu_top_tb.prp) is tracked separately as informational.
//
// vpu_tensora_rf sits in the minion_top cone, so BOTH sim modes reach it —
// the Pyrope tree directly, and the slang re-emission of minion/verilog.
//
// The write path is preview-gated: wr_en_early_i opens the preview latch that
// captures wr_data_i, and wr_en_i commits it into the array. Holding all three
// steady drives entry 0 to the written value, which the async read port
// returns.
//
// STATUS: the minion sim scenarios PASS — this is a real elaborate + cgen +
// host-compile + run smoke, and the RF reads back 0x1234 (bench/sim.sh gates
// on the "hello world" line AND the printed value, via CORE_SIM_EXPECT
// data=4660). Minion is pervasively latch-based (preview/commit RFs) and NO
// module in the vpu_top cone has a latch-free sub-cone, so this module is
// also the only shape available — do not "fix" this file by picking another
// module or by loosening the gate.
//
// One limitation remains (fixme.md issue 2): the comptime evaluator that
// folds the testbench does not model this RF's transparent latch + negedge
// (posclk=false) flop, so an `assert` on the read-back value folds to a
// comptime-false failure before cgen is reached. That is why the value is
// printed rather than asserted. The runtime is now trustworthy on this shape
// — it computes 4660 while the fold still claims false — so restoring the
// assert is blocked only on the fold learning to decline.
//
// (The other half of this note used to describe a silent miscompile: the
// latch -> negedge-flop enable got an /*UNRESOLVED-CYCLE*/ constant-false
// commit guard and the RF read back 0. Fixed in cgen_sim.cpp; regression is
// livehd's inou/prp/tests/sim/latch_sim_negedge_enable.prp.)
//
// Usage: copy next to a Pyrope tree of the design (minion/pyrope, or a slang
// re-emission of minion/verilog), then:  lhd sim <dir>/tensora_rf_tb.prp
const rf = import("vpu_tensora_rf.vpu_tensora_rf")

test rf.hello(cycles:u20 = 1000) {
  mut acc = rf
  mut got = 0
  tick cycles clocks=(clock=1) {
    acc.wr_data_i = 0x1234
    acc.wr_en_early_i = 1
    acc.wr_en_i = 1
    acc.wr_addr_i = 0
    acc.rd_addr_i = 0
    step
    got = acc.rd_data_o
  }
  puts("hello world: minion vpu_tensora_rf ran {cycles} cycles, data={got}")
}
